/P 74 0 R
/E (360-degree feedback is an important modern approach to performance evaluation and employee development. Unlike traditional supervisor-only evaluation, it collects feedback from multiple sources such as managers, peers, subordinates and sometimes customers and the employees themselves.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (The major strength of 360-degree feedback is that it provides different perspectives on an employee's performance and behaviour. It can improve self-awareness, identify development needs and support leadership development.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (However, 360-degree feedback is not automatically effective in every situation. The quality of the process depends on factors such as the selection of raters, confidentiality, clear evaluation criteria, employee acceptance and proper follow-up.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
